"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[9073],{9073:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"samolet-tekhdefolt-reyting-gendirektor","locale":"en","title":"In one month, developer Samolet delays a bond payment, receives 2 downgrades and loses its chief executive","description":"Samolet recorded a technical default, 2 agencies cut its rating to BBB, and its chief executive is leaving after EU sanctions. What this means for buyers and investors.","blocks":[{"id":"b001","kind":"paragraph","text":"In late September 2026, Samolet Group delayed redemption of a 2.5 billion ruble bond issue by one day, attributing it to a transfer delay. This is called a technical default: the company has funds but the payment does not arrive on time. ACRA subsequently cut Samolet\'s credit rating to BBB with a negative outlook. NCR followed on October 15, lowering its rating from A."},{"id":"b002","kind":"paragraph","text":"A credit rating indicates how likely a company is to repay debt. It resembles a person\'s credit history: the worse it is, the higher the interest on new borrowing. NCR cited increased leverage, weaker debt-servicing metrics and lower profitability. Its negative outlook reflected tighter mortgage programs: when mortgages become more expensive, apartments sell less readily and developers find debt harder to service."},{"id":"b003","kind":"paragraph","text":"In mid-October, the EU sanctioned Samolet and chief executive Anna Akinshina, citing North Korean workers at Vladivostok construction sites, which it regards as violating UN sanctions from 2017. On October 16, the company said Akinshina was leaving for personal reasons. Ivan Ivanov, head of Samolet Select, will be proposed as her replacement. Another 2 board members resigned; their names were not disclosed."},{"id":"b004","kind":"paragraph","text":"Sberbank is Samolet\'s largest creditor, with a 274.2 billion ruble loan portfolio at the company. First deputy chairman Alexander Vedyakhin said the bank is working with all the developer\'s creditors and preparing an improvement plan. On October 9, the Construction Ministry gathered developers, banks and tax officials and demanded that banks mobilize resources to ensure a major developer completes all its homes. The ministry did not name the company in its statement."},{"id":"b005","kind":"paragraph","text":"The problems did not begin in October. Early in 2026, Samolet asked the government for a subsidized loan of 48–50 billion rubles, but a Finance Ministry subcommittee found no critical problems. Shares sold at the IPO for 950 rubles fell below 300 in July after dividends were canceled. On October 16 they traded around 247.6 rubles, almost 4 times cheaper. Samolet is not exceptional: Expert RA says downgrades represented 8.1% of its rating actions on highly rated real-economy companies over 9 months of 2026, versus 1.8% during all of 2025."},{"id":"b006","kind":"paragraph","text":"Apartment buyers\' main question is whether homes will be completed. The Construction Ministry demands precisely that, and the largest creditor is preparing its own plan, so both authorities and the bank currently favor completion. For bondholders, a downgrade means securities have become riskier and markets demand more interest for that risk. Holding means betting on Sberbank\'s plan; selling now means crystallizing a loss at the lower price. The plan and whether it will arrive before the next payments remain unknown."},{"id":"b007","kind":"heading","text":"What happened to developer Samolet?"},{"id":"b008","kind":"paragraph","text":"In late September 2026, the company delayed redemption of 2.5 billion rubles of bonds by a day. ACRA and NCR then lowered its rating to BBB with negative outlooks, the EU sanctioned the company and its chief executive, and Anna Akinshina announced her departure."},{"id":"b009","kind":"heading","text":"What is a technical default?"},{"id":"b010","kind":"paragraph","text":"A debt-payment delay of a few days when the company has funds but the payment fails to arrive on time. Samolet\'s delay lasted one day and was attributed to transfer timing. Markets still regard it as a warning that funds for payments are tight."},{"id":"b011","kind":"heading","text":"What will happen to Samolet\'s homes?"},{"id":"b012","kind":"paragraph","text":"On October 9, the Construction Ministry demanded that banks mobilize resources so developers can complete homes and fulfill obligations to buyers. Sberbank, Samolet\'s largest creditor, is preparing an improvement plan. Its details have not yet been announced."}],"sources":[{"label":"How many defaults occurred in Russia\'s debt market from October 12 to 16","url":"https://frankmedia.ru/310263"},{"label":"Developer Samolet announces a change of chief executive","url":"https://frankmedia.ru/310548"},{"label":"NCR cuts Samolet\'s rating to BBB following ACRA","url":"https://frankmedia.ru/310395"},{"label":"Sanctioned Russian developer announces a change of chief executive","url":"https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/16/popavvshiy-pod-sanktsii-rossiyskiy-zastroyschik-ob-yavil-o-smene-gendirektora"},{"label":"Authorities demand Russian banks mobilize support for developers","url":"https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/09/mobilizovat"}],"sourceBodySha256":"556c692bc853437d88a15a7dc68acf4d7948a9d61dd5f274aba150be3640471e"}')}}]);